# L §3.1: text: "Nothing computes with it but == and !="; codes are values an input can hold (half-up).
# round(2.5, 1, m) with m = half-up gives 3 (L §7.2 half-up: a tie goes away from zero).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

input name: text
input m: rounding
input x: num
input step: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  name = "Bank Pocztowy"
  m = half-up
  x = 2.5
  step = 1

ask q1: name == "Bank Pocztowy", name != "Bank Pocztowy", m, round(x, step, m)
=== expect
q1: (true, false, half-up, 3)
  cut 2026-01-01
